{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-terumot-8-1-2-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Terumot", "locator": "8:1:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Terumot.8.1.2", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Zeraim/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Terumot/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "הלכה: הָאִשָּׁה שֶׁהָיְתָה אוֹכֶלֶת בִּתְרוּמָה כו׳. נִיחָא מֵת בַּעֲלֵיךְ. גִּירְשָׁךְ. רַבָּנִין אָמְרִין כְּמִשְׁנָה רִאשׁוֹנָה. שֶׁכֵּן אֲרוּסָה בַת יִשְׂרָאֵל אוֹכֶלֶת בִּתְרוּמָה וְאָבִיהָ מְקַבֵּל אֶת גִּיטָּהּ. רִבִּי לִיעֶזֶר אוֹמֵר וַאֲפִילוּ תֵימַר כְּמִשְׁנָה אַחֲרוֹנָה. תִּיפָּתֵר שֶׁאָמְרָה לוֹ הֲבֵא גִיטִּי מִמָּקוֹם פְּלוֹנִי וְהָיָה דַרְכּוֹ לְהָבִיא לָהּ בַּעֲשָׂרָה יָמִים וּמָצָא סוּס רָץ וְהֵבִיא לָהּ לַחֲמִשָּׁה יָמִים. וְלֹא רִבִּי לִיעֶזֶר כְּרִבִּי לָעְזָר. דְּתַנִּינָן רִבִּי לָעְזָר אוֹסֵר מִיַּד. וְלֹא מוֹדֵי רִבִּי לָעְזָר שֶׁאִם אָמְרָה הֲבֵא לִי גִיטִּי מִמָּקוֹם פְּלוֹנִי שֶׁהִיא אוֹכֶלֶת בִּתְרוּמָה עַד שֶׁמַּגִּיעַ גֶּט לְאוֹתוֹ מָקוֹם. אָמַר רִבִּי חֲנַנְיָה מִכֵּיוָן שֶׁאָמְרָה לוֹ הֲבֵא לִי גִיטִּי מִמָּקוֹם פְּלוֹנִי כְּמִי שֶׁאָמְרָה לוֹ לֹא יְהֵא גֶט אֶלָּא לַעֲשָׂרָה יָמִים מַה שֶׁאָכְלָה בְּהֵיתֵר אָכְלָה.", "context": "Complete segment gives a divorce-delivery timing hypothetical: a route normally taking ten days is completed in five after finding a running horse. Rapid ordinary transport affects the terumah rule; no supernatural motion.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment gives a divorce-delivery timing hypothetical: a route normally taking ten days is completed in five after finding a running horse. Rapid ordinary transport affects the terumah rule; no supernatural motion.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-008", "role": "fast_horse_legal_hypothetical", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-yoma-3-2-5-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Yoma", "locator": "3:2:5", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Yoma.3.2.5", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Moed/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Yoma/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "indirect", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "[דִּלֹמָא. רִבִּי חִיָיא רוֹבָא וְרִבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן חֲלַפְתָּא הֲווּ מְהַלְּכִין בְּהָדָא בִקְעַת אַרְבֵּל בַּקְּרִיצְתָּה רָאוּ אַיֶּלֶת הַשַּׁחַר שֶׁבָּקַע אוֹרָהּ. אָמַר רִבִּי חִיָא רוֹבָה לְרִבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן חֲלַפְתָּא. בִּרְבִּי. כָּךְ הִיא גְאולָּתָן שֶׁל יִשְׂרָאֵל. בַּתְּחִילָּה קִימְעָא קִימְעָא. כָּל שֶׁהִיא הוֹלֶכֶת הִיא הוֹלֶכֶת וּמֵאִיר. מַאי טַעֲמָא. כִּי יוֹשֵׁב בַּחשֶׁךְ יְי אוֹר לִי. כַּךְ בַּתְּחִילָּה וּמָרְדֳּכַי יוֹשֵׁב בְּשַׁעַר הַמֶּלֶךְ. וְאָחַר כָּךְ וַיָּשָׁב מָרְדֳּכַי אֶל שַׁעַר הַמֶּלֶךְ. וְאָחַר כָּךְ וַיִּקַּח הָמָן אֶת הַלְּבוּשׁ וְאֶת הַסּוּס. וְאָחַר כָּךְ וּמָרְדֳּכַי יָצָא מִלִּפְנֵי הַמֶּלֶךְ בִּלְבוּשׁ מַלְכוּת. וְאָחַר כָּךְ לַיְּהוּדִים הָיְתָה אוֹרָה וְשִׂמְחָה.", "context": "Complete segment likens Israel's redemption to gradually increasing dawn and lists stages from Esther, including Haman taking the royal garment and horse. Scriptural royal-procession allusion, not supernatural horse travel.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment likens Israel's redemption to gradually increasing dawn and lists stages from Esther, including Haman taking the royal garment and horse. Scriptural royal-procession allusion, not supernatural horse travel.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-008", "role": "esther_royal_horse_redemption_sequence", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-114b-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "114b:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.114b.2", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Kodashim/Chullin/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "הא למה לי קרא, הא אתיא לה? אמר רב אחדבוי בר אמי: משום דאיכא למימר, סוס בן סוסיא אחי פרדה יוכיח, שאסור פרי עם פרי, ומותר פרי עם האם.", "context": "A horse born to a mare and sibling of a mule is introduced as a counterexample in deriving the prohibition of cooking offspring with its mother. Legal analogy, not extraordinary horse lore.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A horse born to a mare and sibling of a mule is introduced as a counterexample in deriving the prohibition of cooking offspring with its mother. Legal analogy, not extraordinary horse lore.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_mule_legal_analogy", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
