{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-nedarim-33a-3-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Nedarim", "locator": "33a:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim.33a.3", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Nashim/Nedarim/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אמר רב פפא: שק להביא פירות, וחמור להביא עליו פירות, ואפילו צנא בעלמא, הנאה המביאה לידי מאכל הוא. בעי רב פפא: סוס לרכוב עליו וטבעת ליראות בה, מהו? מיפסק ומיזל בארעיה, מאי?", "context": "Rav Pappa asks whether lending a horse to ride counts as a benefit that leads to food in vow law. The horse is ordinary transport enabling access.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Rav Pappa asks whether lending a horse to ride counts as a benefit that leads to food in vow law. The horse is ordinary transport enabling access.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_use_as_food_enabling_benefit", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-52a-9-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "52a:9", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.52a.9", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Moed/Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "הסוס בשיר וכו׳. מאי ״יוצאין״? ומאי ״נמשכין״? אמר רב הונא: או יוצאין כרוכין, או נמשכין. ושמואל אמר: יוצאין נמשכין, ואין יוצאין כרוכין.", "context": "The sugya explains whether a horse may go out or be led with its chain/halter on Shabbat. Ordinary restraint law.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The sugya explains whether a horse may go out or be led with its chain/halter on Shabbat. Ordinary restraint law.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_halter_sabbath", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
