{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-64a-13-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "64a:13", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.64a.13", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Moed/Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "indirect", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "ודין הוא: טימא במת וטימא בשרץ. מה כשטימא בשרץ — עשה דבר הבא מזנב הסוס ומזנב הפרה כמעשה עזים, אף כשטימא במת — עשה דבר הבא מזנב הסוס ומזנב הפרה כמעשה עזים.", "context": "An analogy between corpse and creeping-animal impurity asks whether horse- and cow-tail material is treated like goat hair.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "An analogy between corpse and creeping-animal impurity asks whether horse- and cow-tail material is treated like goat hair.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_tail_hair_impurity", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-64a-15-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "64a:15", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.64a.15", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Moed/Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "indirect", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תלמוד לומר: ״בגד״ ו״עור״ ״בגד״ ו״עור״ לגזירה שוה. נאמר ״בגד״ ו״עור״ בשרץ, ונאמר ״בגד״ ו״עור״ במת. מה ״בגד״ ו״עור״ האמור בשרץ — עשה דבר הבא מזנב הסוס ומזנב הפרה כמעשה עזים, אף ״בגד״ ו״עור״ האמור במת — ", "context": "A verbal analogy extends the impurity rule for horse- and cow-tail material from creeping-animal impurity to corpse impurity.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A verbal analogy extends the impurity rule for horse- and cow-tail material from creeping-animal impurity to corpse impurity.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_tail_hair_impurity", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-90b-3-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "90b:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.90b.3", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Moed/Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "indirect", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "זרע קישואין. תנו רבנן: המוציא גרעינין, אם לנטיעה — שתים, אם לאכילה — כמלא פי חזיר, וכמה מלא פי חזיר — אחת. אם להסיק — כדי לבשל ביצה קלה. אם לחשבון — שתים. אחרים אומרים: חמש. תנו רבנן: המוציא שני נימין", "context": "The carrying threshold includes two hairs from a horse’s tail, in a list of small materials and their uses.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The carrying threshold includes two hairs from a horse’s tail, in a list of small materials and their uses.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_tail_hair_carrying_quantity", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-93b-1-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "93b:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.93b.1", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Moed/Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "רבי יוסי אומר: הסוס מטמא על ידיו, החמור — על רגליו, שמשענת הסוס על ידיו, וחמור על רגליו. ואמאי? הא קא מסייע בהדי הדדי! לאו משום דאמרינן מסייע אין בו ממש? אמר רב אשי: אף אנן נמי תנינא. רבי אליעזר אומר:", "context": "R. Yose says a horse transmits impurity through its forelegs because it rests its weight there; the point is used in a discussion of assistance in carrying.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Yose says a horse transmits impurity through its forelegs because it rests its weight there; the point is used in a discussion of assistance in carrying.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_support_and_sabbath_carrying", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-94a-3-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "94a:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.94a.3", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Moed/Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אמר ליה רב אדא בר אהבה לרבא, והא דתנן: בן בתירא מתיר בסוס. ותניא: בן בתירא מתיר בסוס מפני שהוא עושה בו מלאכה שאין חייבין עליו חטאת, ואמר רבי יוחנן: בן בתירא ורבי נתן אמרו דבר אחד. ואי אמרת דלא פליגי ר", "context": "Ben Beteira permits the horse because its characteristic work—carrying a living rider—is treated as work for which one is not liable to a sin offering.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Ben Beteira permits the horse because its characteristic work—carrying a living rider—is treated as work for which one is not liable to a sin offering.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_as_riding_work_exception", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
