{"schema_version": 1, "id": "commentary:Ibn-Ezra:zech-6-8:cell", "corpus_id": "traditional-commentaries", "work": "Ibn Ezra on Zechariah", "locator": "6:8", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Ibn_Ezra_on_Zechariah?context=0&pad=0", "edition": "Sefaria default Hebrew book response; version metadata preserved in COM-004.manifest.json", "language": "he", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "ויזעק, וידבר - המלאך הדובר בו על פי השם, כי השחורים היוצאים אל ארץ צפון עשו נקמת השם בצפון וזה טעם הניחו את רוחי, כמו ומשל ברוחו. וטעם זאת המראה שהודיע הנביא לישראל, כי כל היושב מהם בארץ צפון וירושלם תשכן לבטח.", "context": "Entire saved verse commentary cell read; HTML removed. The black horses execute divine vengeance in the north; the vision reassures Israel that northern exiles and Jerusalem will be secure.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The black horses execute divine vengeance in the north; the vision reassures Israel that northern exiles and Jerusalem will be secure.", "epistemic_type": "traditional_commentary", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "COM-004", "role": "zechariah_horse_vision_interpretation", "limitations": ["Default digital Hebrew response may combine versions; no print/manuscript collation.", "No independent review; historical identifications are preserved as Abarbanel/Ibn Ezra interpretations, not externally verified history."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "parent_reference": "tanakh-wlc-zech-6-8", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
